From a948ecbc70d7225ca0d6db6a94b7127169e36c93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:00:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(windows): walk classic menus without activating the
 window

invoke_menu activated the target to walk its menu and restored foreground
afterwards, 2-4 foreground changes per dialog task. Activation also let the
app keep foreground: a UIA Invoke on a WinForms menu header handed the app
foreground rights, so its next dialog took over the screen.

Now invoke_menu only activates where the menu needs it:
- Win32 menu bars (HMENU): the path is resolved in the menu data and the
  item's WM_COMMAND is posted. The menu never opens (win32/menu.rs).
- Other menus of classic windows (WinForms MenuStrip): every hop is a
  posted click, waiting for each drop-down to show before clicking into it.
- Everything else (WPF, XAML, Win32 menus whose items only exist once
  opened) keeps activate, UIA walk, restore.

The record reports background delivery when the window was not activated,
and structuredContent.windows lists windows the command opened or closed.
